{"name":"Tiger Cat","hex":"#cda035","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tiger cat","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several species of felids:\nAn oncilla (Leopardus tigrinus).\nA margay (Leopardus wiedii).\nAn ocelot (Leopardus pardalis).\nA serval (Leptailurus serval).","An oncilla (Leopardus tigrinus)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tiger_cat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tigercat (sailboat)","blocks":[{"text":"Tigercat was a 1960s catamaran sailboat of the Eastern Multihull Sailing Association. In 1961 it was defeated by John Fisk sailing Hellcats II of the Clapham Sands Sailing Club four races to one."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tigercat_(sailboat)"},{"title":"Hamilton Tiger-Cats","blocks":[{"text":"The Hamilton Tiger-Cats are a professional Canadian football team based in Hamilton, Ontario, Canada. They are currently members of the East Division of the Canadian Football League (CFL). The Tiger-Cats play their home games at Hamilton Stadium."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b4/Hamilton_Tiger-Cats_logo.svg/330px-Hamilton_Tiger-Cats_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamilton_Tiger-Cats"},{"title":"Oncilla","blocks":[{"text":"The oncilla, also known as the northern tiger cat, little spotted cat, and tigrillo, is a small spotted cat ranging from Central America to central Brazil. It is listed as Vulnerable on the IUCN Red List, and the population is threatened by deforestation and conversion of habitat to agricultural land."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Snethlage%27s_Tigrina_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_354017009_on_2_August_2024_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Snethlage%27s_Tigrina_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_354017009_on_2_August_2024_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.o